#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0060_000_0
#. timeline 2479..3260
#: codec/1/166/0xa6910/2
msgid ""
"The basic CO-OPS unit is a two-man cell.\n"
msgstr ""
"CO-OPS的基本单位是双人小组。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0060_000_0
#. timeline 3287..4304
#: codec/1/166/0xa6910/3
msgid ""
"Even a single teammate is great to have in enemy\n"
"territory.\n"
msgstr ""
"在敌占区哪怕只有一个队友\n"
"也强得多。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0060_000_0
#. timeline 4318..5308
#: codec/1/166/0xa6910/4
msgid ""
"And there are actually quite a few things you can't\n"
"do by yourself.\n"
msgstr ""
"而且有些事一个人\n"
"还真做不了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0060_000_0
#. timeline 5335..6311
#: codec/1/166/0xa6910/5
msgid ""
"You can help each other climb walls, divide up\n"
"mission roles...\n"
msgstr ""
"可以互相帮忙爬墙、\n"
"分工执行任务……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0060_000_0
#. timeline 6394..7634
#: codec/1/166/0xa6910/6
msgid ""
"On the other hand, if one of you is spotted, the\n"
"other one's screwed, too.\n"
msgstr ""
"但反过来说，一人被发现，\n"
"另一个也完了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0060_000_0
#. timeline 7648..8665
#: codec/1/166/0xa6910/7
msgid ""
"And it's kind of tough for two people to hide in one\n"
"small space.\n"
msgstr ""
"而且两个人挤一个小地方\n"
"挺难的。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0060_000_0
#. timeline 8679..9626
#: codec/1/166/0xa6910/8
msgid ""
"Good point. But what's more important than\n"
"anything\n"
msgstr ""
"说得好。但比\n"
"什么都\n"
"更重要"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0060_000_0
#. timeline 9626..10309
#: codec/1/166/0xa6910/9
msgid ""
"is how close you are to your comrades.\n"
msgstr ""
"是你和同伴的默契。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0060_000_0
#. timeline 10309..11674
#: codec/1/166/0xa6910/10
msgid ""
"Well said. Working as a two-man cell can make the\n"
"mission easier or harder\n"
msgstr ""
"没错。双人小组能让任务\n"
"变简单还是变难\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0060_000_0
#. timeline 11674..12357
#: codec/1/166/0xa6910/11
msgid ""
"depending on how well you work together.\n"
msgstr ""
"全看你们配合得如何。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0060_000_0
#. timeline 12427..13569
#: codec/1/166/0xa6910/12
msgid ""
"It's also good to note that if you've got a clear,\n"
"specific objective,\n"
msgstr ""
"还有，如果你有清晰、\n"
"具体的目标，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0060_000_0
#. timeline 13583..14558
#: codec/1/166/0xa6910/13
msgid ""
"it can be to your advantage to use an even bigger\n"
"team.\n"
msgstr ""
"使用更大的\n"
"队伍可能对你有利。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0060_000_0
#. timeline 14600..16021
#: codec/1/166/0xa6910/14
msgid ""
"That said, teams of three or more run a much\n"
"greater risk of being spotted.\n"
msgstr ""
"不过三人以上的队伍被发现的\n"
"风险会大得多。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0060_000_0
#. timeline 16035..17303
#: codec/1/166/0xa6910/15
msgid ""
"Yeah. In a sneaking mission, the fewer people you\n"
"have,\n"
msgstr ""
"是啊。在潜行任务中，人越少\n"
"越好，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0060_000_0
#. timeline 17303..17902
#: codec/1/166/0xa6910/16
msgid ""
"the easier it is to get around.\n"
msgstr ""
"行动越方便。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0070_000_0
#. timeline 459..1518
#: codec/1/166/0xa6f50/0
msgid ""
"In CO-OPS, you can trade weapons and equipment\n"
"with your teammates.\n"
msgstr ""
"在联机合作中，你可以和队友\n"
"交换武器与装备。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0070_000_0
#. timeline 1616..2953
#: codec/1/166/0xa6f50/1
msgid ""
"You can also display your teammates' inventories\n"
"from your Weapon or Equipment Menu.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0070_000_0
#. timeline 3009..3566
#: codec/1/166/0xa6f50/2
msgid ""
"Ammo is shared, too, of course.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0070_000_0
#. timeline 3580..4639
#: codec/1/166/0xa6f50/3
msgid ""
"Ammo, sure. How about LIFE? That also shared?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0070_000_0
#. timeline 4653..6102
#: codec/1/166/0xa6f50/4
msgid ""
"Yep. You all sink or swim together. Your teammate\n"
"dies, you die.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0070_000_0
#. timeline 6213..7272
#: codec/1/166/0xa6f50/5
msgid ""
"You need to be within a certain distance of each\n"
"other to swap items.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0070_000_0
#. timeline 7342..8916
#: codec/1/166/0xa6f50/6
msgid ""
"Yeah, I know. I've been in this business so long, I\n"
"can virtually see that distance.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0070_000_0
#. timeline 8930..9515
#: codec/1/166/0xa6f50/7
msgid ""
"Looks kind of like a ring in my head.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0070_000_0
#. timeline 9529..9961
#: codec/1/166/0xa6f50/8
msgid ""
"That's why you're the Boss.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0070_000_0
#. timeline 9989..11591
#: codec/1/166/0xa6f50/9
msgid ""
"OK, we'll call it the \"CO-OP Ring,\" and entering the\n"
"ring will be called going \"CO-OP IN.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0080_000_0
#. timeline 445..1866
#: codec/1/167/0xa7370/0
msgid ""
"Another thing - during a mission you can assume\n"
"what we'll call the Snake Formation.\n"
msgstr ""
"还有一点——任务中可以组成\n"
"所谓的SNAKE阵形。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0080_000_0
#. timeline 1894..2995
#: codec/1/167/0xa7370/1
msgid ""
"Same as your code name - but probably not\n"
"standard operating procedure\n"
msgstr ""
"和代号一样，但对\n"
"单打独斗的人\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0080_000_0
#. timeline 2995..3845
#: codec/1/167/0xa7370/2
msgid ""
"for a guy who specializes in going solo.\n"
msgstr ""
"大概不算标准战术。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0080_000_0
#. timeline 3845..4904
#: codec/1/167/0xa7370/3
msgid ""
"Damn right. There's only room for one Snake.\n"
msgstr ""
"没错。SNAKE只能有一个。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0080_000_0
#. timeline 4931..5851
#: codec/1/167/0xa7370/4
msgid ""
"In CO-OPS, though, it's a highly effective formation.\n"
msgstr ""
"合作任务里，这阵形很有效。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0080_000_0
#. timeline 5851..6979
#: codec/1/167/0xa7370/5
msgid ""
"The signal for Snake Formation is to tap your\n"
"teammate on the shoulder.\n"
msgstr ""
"SNAKE阵形的信号是拍一下\n"
"队友的肩膀。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0080_000_0
#. timeline 7244..8512
#: codec/1/167/0xa7370/6
msgid ""
"Can't form up until you're close enough to reach\n"
"out and touch someone.\n"
msgstr ""
"得靠近到能伸手碰到人\n"
"才能组队。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0080_000_0
#. timeline 8526..9501
#: codec/1/167/0xa7370/7
msgid ""
"Entering Snake Formation is called going \"Snake In.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"进入SNAKE阵形叫“Snake In”。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0080_000_0
#. timeline 9529..10755
#: codec/1/167/0xa7370/8
msgid ""
"When you're Snake In, the soldier at the front of\n"
"the line controls movement.\n"
msgstr ""
"Snake In时，队首的士兵\n"
"负责控制移动。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0080_000_0
#. timeline 10797..11842
#: codec/1/167/0xa7370/9
msgid ""
"The soldiers in back focus on scouting and attack.\n"
msgstr ""
"后面的士兵专注侦察和攻击。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0090_000_0
#. timeline 445..1448
#: codec/1/167/0xa7780/0
msgid ""
"Just because your heart stops doesn't mean you're\n"
"dead immediately.\n"
msgstr ""
"心脏停止跳动并不意味着你会\n"
"立刻死亡。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0090_000_0
#. timeline 1476..2521
#: codec/1/167/0xa7780/1
msgid ""
"Right. The heart just circulates blood through the\n"
"body.\n"
msgstr ""
"对。心脏只是负责让血液\n"
"在体内循环。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0090_000_0
#. timeline 2549..4221
#: codec/1/167/0xa7780/2
msgid ""
"But stopping it does cut oxygen supply to the\n"
"brain - you'll be dead soon after.\n"
msgstr ""
"但停跳会切断大脑的氧气供应——\n"
"很快就会死。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0090_000_0
#. timeline 4249..4862
#: codec/1/167/0xa7780/3
msgid ""
"Which is why we have CPR.\n"
msgstr ""
"所以要心肺复苏。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0090_000_0
#. timeline 4904..5419
#: codec/1/167/0xa7780/4
msgid ""
"Let's say your heart does stop.\n"
msgstr ""
"假设你的心脏停跳了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0090_000_0
#. timeline 5419..6770
#: codec/1/167/0xa7780/5
msgid ""
"If someone performs CPR before your brain cells\n"
"die you can recover.\n"
msgstr ""
"脑细胞死前有人做心肺复苏，\n"
"你就能恢复。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0090_000_0
#. timeline 6826..7871
#: codec/1/167/0xa7780/6
msgid ""
"In CO-OPS, when the LIFE Gauge drops to zero,\n"
msgstr ""
"合作任务中，生命值降到零时，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0090_000_0
#. timeline 7871..8498
#: codec/1/167/0xa7780/7
msgid ""
"it means you're in a near-death state.\n"
msgstr ""
"意味着你处于濒死状态。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0090_000_0
#. timeline 8498..9250
#: codec/1/167/0xa7780/8
msgid ""
"You won't be able to move or anything else.\n"
msgstr ""
"你将无法移动或做任何事。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0090_000_0
#. timeline 9264..10574
#: codec/1/167/0xa7780/9
msgid ""
"Performing CPR on near-death teammates can\n"
"bring them back into action.\n"
msgstr ""
"对濒死的队友做心肺复苏\n"
"能让他们重返战斗。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0090_000_0
#. timeline 10616..11828
#: codec/1/167/0xa7780/10
msgid ""
"Of course, performing CPR in the middle of battle\n"
"isn't exactly safe.\n"
msgstr ""
"当然，在战斗中做心肺复苏\n"
"并不安全。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0090_000_0
#. timeline 11842..12427
#: codec/1/167/0xa7780/11
msgid ""
"You're leaving yourself exposed.\n"
msgstr ""
"你把自己暴露了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0090_000_0
#. timeline 12455..13820
#: codec/1/167/0xa7780/12
msgid ""
"Even so, in CO-OPS you and your teammates are\n"
"all in the same boat.\n"
msgstr ""
"但合作任务里你和队友\n"
"同舟共济。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0090_000_0
#. timeline 13820..14684
#: codec/1/167/0xa7780/13
msgid ""
"Don't think you can get away with leaving one of\n"
"them behind.\n"
msgstr ""
"别以为丢下他们中的谁\n"
"能没事。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0090_000_0
#. timeline 14712..16035
#: codec/1/167/0xa7780/14
msgid ""
"I wouldn't think of it. And I'd expect them to do the\n"
"same for me.\n"
msgstr ""
"我不会那么想。我也指望他们\n"
"同样对我。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0090_000_0
#. timeline 16049..16927
#: codec/1/167/0xa7780/15
msgid ""
"If you let all your teammates die during a mission,\n"
msgstr ""
"如果任务中你让所有队友都死了，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0090_000_0
#. timeline 16955..17540
#: codec/1/167/0xa7780/16
msgid ""
"there'll be nobody left to save you.\n"
msgstr ""
"就没人能来救你了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0090_000_0
#. timeline 17540..18320
#: codec/1/167/0xa7780/17
msgid ""
"And then it's game over.\n"
msgstr ""
"然后就结束了。\n"

#: codec/1/167/0xa7dc0/0
msgid ""
"Building trust with your teammates is essential to\n"
"success in CO-OPS.\n"
msgstr ""
"与队友建立信任，是联机合作\n"
"取胜的关键。\n"

#: codec/1/167/0xa7dc0/1
msgid ""
"That goes without saying.\n"
msgstr ""
"那还用说。\n"

#: codec/1/167/0xa7dc0/2
msgid ""
"I'm not gonna let somebody I can't trust cover my\n"
"ass.\n"
msgstr ""
"我可不会让信不过的人\n"
"掩护我。\n"

#: codec/1/167/0xa7dc0/3
msgid ""
"The measure of that trust is called \"camaraderie.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"衡量这种信任的指标叫「战友情」。\n"

#: codec/1/167/0xa7dc0/4
msgid ""
"Think of it as an indicator of how strong your bond\n"
"is with your CO-OPS teammates.\n"
msgstr ""
"可以把它看作你与联机队友\n"
"羁绊强弱的指标。\n"

#: codec/1/167/0xa7dc0/5
msgid ""
"The friendlier you act toward them, the greater\n"
"your camaraderie.\n"
msgstr ""
"你对他们越友善，\n"
"战友情就越高。\n"

#: codec/1/167/0xa7dc0/6
msgid ""
"Give me an example.\n"
msgstr ""
"举个例子。\n"

#: codec/1/167/0xa7dc0/7
msgid ""
"Your camaraderie will be higher if you're \"CO-OP In\"\n"
"than standing apart.\n"
msgstr ""
"保持「联机待命」时的战友情，\n"
"会比各自为战更高。\n"

#: codec/1/167/0xa7dc0/8
msgid ""
"Saving a teammate's life with CPR also strengthens\n"
"your bonds with them.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/167/0xa7dc0/9
msgid ""
"Things like hitting a teammate with friendly fire\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/167/0xa7dc0/10
msgid ""
"will cause your camaraderie to go down.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/167/0xa7dc0/11
msgid ""
"Makes sense.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/167/0xa7dc0/12
msgid ""
"Camaraderie carries over from mission to mission.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/167/0xa7dc0/13
msgid ""
"The next time you go CO-OPS In with the same\n"
"guy, you'll start off strong.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/167/0xa7dc0/14
msgid ""
"But be careful. If you keep taking new people with\n"
"you on missions,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/167/0xa7dc0/15
msgid ""
"your camaraderie with past teammates eventually\n"
"reverts back to its original level.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/167/0xa7dc0/16
msgid ""
"Got it. I'll have to make sure to renew old\n"
"friendships once in a while.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/167/0xa7dc0/17
msgid ""
"The performance benefits gained from Snake Sync\n"
"in CO-OPS\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/167/0xa7dc0/18
#: codec/1/168/0xa84e0/9
msgid ""
"depend on your camaraderie.\n"
msgstr ""
"取决于战友情。\n"

#: codec/1/167/0xa7dc0/19
msgid ""
"It's always best to keep things cool with your\n"
"teammates.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/168/0xa84e0/0
msgid ""
"Stand still when you're Snake In and you and your\n"
"teammates will start to get in sync.\n"
msgstr ""
"SNAKE IN时站住不动，你和队友\n"
"就会开始同步。\n"

#: codec/1/168/0xa84e0/1
msgid ""
"In sync?\n"
msgstr ""
"同步？\n"

#: codec/1/168/0xa84e0/2
msgid ""
"That's right. Stay still together and you'll enter\n"
"Snake Sync mode.\n"
msgstr ""
"没错。一起站住不动，就会进入\n"
"SNAKE同步模式。\n"

#: codec/1/168/0xa84e0/3
msgid ""
"The synergy will give you a boost in performance.\n"
msgstr ""
"协同效应会提升你的表现。\n"

#: codec/1/168/0xa84e0/4
msgid ""
"You'll move faster, recover faster, and have better\n"
"camouflage.\n"
msgstr ""
"移动更快，恢复更快，伪装\n"
"也更好。\n"

#: codec/1/168/0xa84e0/5
msgid ""
"In other words, we're at our best when we're in the\n"
"same groove.\n"
msgstr ""
"就是说，步调一致时\n"
"我们最强。\n"

#: codec/1/168/0xa84e0/6
msgid ""
"You got it. If you've got a big task ahead,\n"
msgstr ""
"明白了。如果前面有艰巨任务，\n"

#: codec/1/168/0xa84e0/7
msgid ""
"it can't hurt to take some time to get in sync.\n"
msgstr ""
"花点时间同步没坏处。\n"

#: codec/1/168/0xa84e0/8
msgid ""
"Like I said before, the benefits you get from Snake\n"
"Sync\n"
msgstr ""
"就像我之前说的，你从Snake\n"
"Sync获得的好处\n"

#: codec/1/168/0xa84e0/10
msgid ""
"I hear ya.\n"
msgstr ""
"我懂。\n"

#: codec/1/168/0xa84e0/11
msgid ""
"It's a lot easier knowing you've got someone you\n"
"know and trust covering your back.\n"
msgstr ""
"知道有信得过的人替你掩护，\n"
"会轻松很多。\n"

#: codec/1/168/0xa84e0/12
msgid ""
"It lets you focus that much more on what you have\n"
"to do.\n"
msgstr ""
"它能让你更加专注于你必须\n"
"要做的事情。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0110_000_0
#. timeline 445..1407
#: codec/1/168/0xa8980/0
msgid ""
"If camaraderie represents how much your\n"
"teammates trust you,\n"
msgstr ""
"战友情谊代表\n"
"队友对你的信任，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0110_000_0
#. timeline 1421..2298
#: codec/1/168/0xa8980/1
msgid ""
"then heroism shows how high your reputation is.\n"
msgstr ""
"那英雄度就代表你的声望有多高。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0110_000_0
#. timeline 2312..2688
#: codec/1/168/0xa8980/2
msgid ""
"\"Heroism?\"\n"
msgstr ""
"“英雄度？”\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0110_000_0
#. timeline 2702..3246
#: codec/1/168/0xa8980/3
msgid ""
"That's right, heroism.\n"
msgstr ""
"没错，英雄度。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0110_000_0
#. timeline 3274..4583
#: codec/1/168/0xa8980/4
msgid ""
"Your reputation affects your ability to recruit new\n"
"members to MSF.\n"
msgstr ""
"你的声望影响你招募新成员\n"
"加入MSF的能力。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0110_000_0
#. timeline 4611..5948
#: codec/1/168/0xa8980/5
msgid ""
"With higher heroism, it won't take as long to\n"
"convince guys to join our cause\n"
msgstr ""
"英雄度越高，说服别人加入\n"
"就越快\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0110_000_0
#. timeline 5948..6673
#: codec/1/168/0xa8980/6
msgid ""
"and send 'em back by Fulton recovery.\n"
msgstr ""
"再用富尔顿回收送回来。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0110_000_0
#. timeline 6854..7857
#: codec/1/168/0xa8980/7
msgid ""
"So how do I get this \"heroism\" thing to go up?\n"
msgstr ""
"那怎么提升这个“英雄度”？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0110_000_0
#. timeline 7871..9292
#: codec/1/168/0xa8980/8
msgid ""
"Lots of ways. Complete tough missions. Avoid\n"
"unnecessary bloodshed...\n"
msgstr ""
"方法很多。完成高难任务。避免\n"
"无谓杀戮……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0110_000_0
#. timeline 9292..10685
#: codec/1/168/0xa8980/9
msgid ""
"And don't get caught by the enemy like a deer in\n"
"headlights, or you'll never be heroic.\n"
msgstr ""
"别像被车灯照到的鹿一样被敌人抓住，\n"
"否则永远当不了英雄。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0110_000_0
#. timeline 10699..11647
#: codec/1/168/0xa8980/10
msgid ""
"Also, getting out there and attacking the enemy in\n"
"CO-OPS\n"
msgstr ""
"还有，主动出击，在\n"
"合作模式中打敌人\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0110_000_0
#. timeline 11647..12455
#: codec/1/168/0xa8980/11
msgid ""
"will boost your reputation among your teammates.\n"
msgstr ""
"能提升你在队友中的声望。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0110_000_0
#. timeline 12483..13444
#: codec/1/168/0xa8980/12
msgid ""
"Of course, it'll get the enemy gunning right for you,\n"
"too.\n"
msgstr ""
"当然，这也会让敌人把枪口\n"
"对准你。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0110_000_0
#. timeline 13500..14140
#: codec/1/168/0xa8980/13
msgid ""
"But don't sweat it. Be yourself.\n"
msgstr ""
"别紧张。做你自己。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0110_000_0
#. timeline 14154..15520
#: codec/1/168/0xa8980/14
msgid ""
"Be the Boss. From where I'm standing, you're\n"
"plenty heroic already.\n"
msgstr ""
"做BOSS。在我看来，你已经\n"
"够英雄了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0110_000_0
#. timeline 15520..15938
#: codec/1/168/0xa8980/15
msgid ""
"Knock it off.\n"
msgstr ""
"少来。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0120_000_1
#. timeline 445..1685
#: codec/1/168/0xa8f00/0
msgid ""
"Seems the R&D team's been busy working on CO-OPS\n"
"only weapons.\n"
msgstr ""
"研发组似乎一直在忙着做\n"
"联机专用的武器。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0120_000_1
#. timeline 1699..2131
#: codec/1/168/0xa8f00/1
msgid ""
"CO-OPS only?\n"
msgstr ""
"联机专用？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0120_000_1
#. timeline 2145..2883
#: codec/1/168/0xa8f00/2
msgid ""
"Like a gun with extreme firepower...\n"
msgstr ""
"比如火力极其凶猛的枪……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0120_000_1
#. timeline 2897..4304
#: codec/1/168/0xa8f00/3
msgid ""
"But only when two people fire it at once. I hear it's\n"
"still in the concept stage.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0120_000_1
#. timeline 4374..5224
#: codec/1/168/0xa8f00/4
msgid ""
"I know some rocket launchers need two people to\n"
"operate,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0120_000_1
#. timeline 5224..6004
#: codec/1/168/0xa8f00/5
msgid ""
"but a CO-OPS only weapon...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0120_000_1
#. timeline 6018..6534
#: codec/1/168/0xa8f00/6
msgid ""
"Hey, if they come up with something good,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0120_000_1
#. timeline 6534..7258
#: codec/1/168/0xa8f00/7
msgid ""
"you'll have that much more reason to go CO-OPS.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0120_000_1
#. timeline 7314..8219
#: codec/1/168/0xa8f00/8
msgid ""
"Why don't you check in and see how they're doing\n"
"every once in a while?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/169/0xa9240/0
msgid ""
"In CO-OPS, maintaining close communications with\n"
"your teammates is crucial.\n"
msgstr ""
"合作任务中，与队友保持紧密通讯\n"
"至关重要。\n"

#: codec/1/169/0xa9240/1
msgid ""
"Absolutely. Losing track of each other on the\n"
"battlefield is a good way\n"
msgstr ""
"没错。在战场上失去彼此的踪迹\n"
"是个好办法\n"

#: codec/1/169/0xa9240/2
msgid ""
"for a unit to get itself wiped out.\n"
msgstr ""
"整支部队就会被全灭。\n"

#: codec/1/169/0xa9240/3
msgid ""
"Enemy positions. Orders. Distress calls.\n"
msgstr ""
"敌情。命令。求救。\n"

#: codec/1/169/0xa9240/4
msgid ""
"When communications break down, you get picked\n"
"off one by one.\n"
msgstr ""
"当通讯中断时，你会被\n"
"逐个击破。\n"

#: codec/1/169/0xa9240/5
msgid ""
"Now, about CO-OPS Comms.\n"
msgstr ""
"说说合作通讯。\n"

#: codec/1/169/0xa9240/6
msgid ""
"CO-OPS Comms…\n"
msgstr ""
"合作通讯…\n"

#: codec/1/169/0xa9240/7
msgid ""
"It's a radio system for communicating with CO-OPS\n"
"teammates.\n"
msgstr ""
"这是与合作模式\n"
"队友通讯的无线电。\n"

#: codec/1/169/0xa9240/8
msgid ""
"First open the menu, then select \"CO-OPS Comms.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"先打开菜单，选择“合作通讯”。\n"

#: codec/1/169/0xa9240/9
msgid ""
"After that, press one button to choose a category,\n"
msgstr ""
"然后按一个键选类别，\n"

#: codec/1/169/0xa9240/10
msgid ""
"then another button to select the actual message.\n"
msgstr ""
"再按另一个键选具体讯息。\n"

#: codec/1/169/0xa9240/11
msgid ""
"So basically you use different combinations of two\n"
"buttons\n"
msgstr ""
"所以基本上，你使用两个按键的\n"
"不同组合\n"

#: codec/1/169/0xa9240/12
msgid ""
"to send different messages.\n"
msgstr ""
"发送不同讯息。\n"

#: codec/1/169/0xa9240/13
msgid ""
"Easy enough.\n"
msgstr ""
"简单。\n"

#: codec/1/169/0xa9240/14
msgid ""
"You can set which messages go with which\n"
"buttons during mission prep.\n"
msgstr ""
"任务准备时可设定各按键对应的\n"
"讯息。\n"

#: codec/1/169/0xa9240/15
msgid ""
"Sounds like it's going to be a pain to send\n"
"messages until I get used to it.\n"
msgstr ""
"感觉在习惯之前发送讯息\n"
"会很麻烦。\n"

#: codec/1/169/0xa9240/16
msgid ""
"Then why don't you assign CO-OPS Comms to\n"
"whatever button you like?\n"
msgstr ""
"那不如把合作任务通讯设到\n"
"你喜欢的按键上？\n"

#: codec/1/169/0xa9240/17
msgid ""
"That should make things a little quicker and easier.\n"
msgstr ""
"这样应该会更快更轻松。\n"

#: codec/1/169/0xa9240/18
msgid ""
"Just go to \"Key Config\".\n"
msgstr ""
"进\"按键配置\"。\n"

#: codec/1/169/0xa9240/19
msgid ""
"I'll give it a try.\n"
msgstr ""
"我试试看。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0130_010_1
#. timeline 473..1588
#: codec/1/169/0xa98c0/0
msgid ""
"Snake, you familiar with the Japanese word\n"
"\"kotodama\"?\n"
msgstr ""
"SNAKE，你听过日本的\n"
"\"言灵\"这个词吗？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0130_010_1
#. timeline 1880..2368
#: codec/1/169/0xa98c0/1
msgid ""
"Kotodama...?\n"
msgstr ""
"言灵？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0130_010_1
#. timeline 2382..3329
#: codec/1/169/0xa98c0/2
msgid ""
"Unfortunately, there's no direct equivalent in\n"
"English...\n"
msgstr ""
"很遗憾，英文里没有直接对应的\n"
"说法……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0130_010_1
#. timeline 3329..4458
#: codec/1/169/0xa98c0/3
msgid ""
"But to keep it simple, let's call it a sort of \"Battle\n"
"Cry.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"但简单来说，我们就叫它一种“战\n"
"吼”吧。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0130_010_1
#. timeline 4527..5029
#: codec/1/169/0xa98c0/4
msgid ""
"\"Battle Cry,\" huh?\n"
msgstr ""
"\"战吼\"啊。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0130_010_1
#. timeline 5071..6436
#: codec/1/169/0xa98c0/5
msgid ""
"Right. But, Kotodama is actually a deep Japanese\n"
"concept.\n"
msgstr ""
"没错。但言灵其实是日本很深的\n"
"概念。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0130_010_1
#. timeline 6561..7565
#: codec/1/169/0xa98c0/6
msgid ""
"\"Koto\" means word, and \"dama\" means spirit.\n"
msgstr ""
"\"言\"是词语，\"灵\"是灵魂。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0130_010_1
#. timeline 7578..8791
#: codec/1/169/0xa98c0/7
msgid ""
"It signifies that words have power that affect our\n"
"reality...\n"
msgstr ""
"它意味着言语拥有影响我们\n"
"现实的力量……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0130_010_1
#. timeline 9306..10128
#: codec/1/169/0xa98c0/8
msgid ""
"Ah... You feeling OK?\n"
msgstr ""
"呃……你没事吧？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0130_010_1
#. timeline 10128..11103
#: codec/1/169/0xa98c0/9
msgid ""
"Guess I made it sound kind of like mumbo-jumbo,\n"
"huh.\n"
msgstr ""
"看来我说得有点像迷信了，\n"
"是吧。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0130_010_1
#. timeline 11229..12580
#: codec/1/169/0xa98c0/10
msgid ""
"Seriously, though, haven't you ever felt energized\n"
"when a teammate cheered you on?\n"
msgstr ""
"不过说真的，队友为你加油时\n"
"你没觉得浑身是劲吗？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0130_010_1
#. timeline 12580..14168
#: codec/1/169/0xa98c0/11
msgid ""
"Or - the other way around - ever had your legs cut\n"
"out from under you by a thoughtless remark?\n"
msgstr ""
"反过来，一句无心之言\n"
"也可能让你泄气。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0130_010_1
#. timeline 14349..15645
#: codec/1/169/0xa98c0/12
msgid ""
"I know the feeling. Words can have a powerful\n"
"mental effect on people.\n"
msgstr ""
"我懂。话语能对人的心理\n"
"产生巨大影响。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0130_010_1
#. timeline 15659..16272
#: codec/1/169/0xa98c0/13
msgid ""
"Same goes for CO-OPS Comms.\n"
msgstr ""
"合作通讯也一样。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0130_010_1
#. timeline 16300..17359
#: codec/1/169/0xa98c0/14
msgid ""
"Offering praise to somebody could make them run\n"
"faster than usual.\n"
msgstr ""
"对某人给予赞扬可能会让他们跑得\n"
"比平时更快。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0130_010_1
#. timeline 17373..18822
#: codec/1/169/0xa98c0/15
msgid ""
"Or make somebody who thinks they're done for get\n"
"up and fight again... See what I'm saying?\n"
msgstr ""
"也能让以为没救的人重新站起来战斗……\n"
"明白吗？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0130_010_1
#. timeline 18822..19825
#: codec/1/169/0xa98c0/16
msgid ""
"I get the picture. So it works in reverse, too.\n"
msgstr ""
"我懂了。所以反过来也成立。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0130_010_1
#. timeline 19853..21329
#: codec/1/169/0xa98c0/17
msgid ""
"The powers of words are many and varied. Try\n"
"using them for yourself.\n"
msgstr ""
"话语的力量多种多样。你自己\n"
"也试试看吧。\n"

#: codec/1/169/0xa9f40/0
msgid ""
"Snake, about cardboard boxes...\n"
msgstr ""
"Snake，关于纸箱……\n"

#: codec/1/169/0xa9f40/1
msgid ""
"Ahh!\n"
msgstr ""
"啊！\n"

#: codec/1/169/0xa9f40/2
msgid ""
"It feels kind of weird, me explaining this stuff to\n"
"you,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/169/0xa9f40/3
msgid ""
"but there've been a few recent developments in\n"
"cardboard box technology.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/169/0xa9f40/4
msgid ""
"So, just to be safe here goes...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/169/0xa9f40/5
msgid ""
"Go on...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/169/0xa9f40/6
msgid ""
"You can do much more with a box than just hide\n"
"under it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/169/0xa9f40/7
msgid ""
"You can put it someplace and leave it there.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/169/0xa9f40/8
msgid ""
"Huh!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/169/0xa9f40/9
msgid ""
"You can get on top of it and use it to reach high\n"
"places,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/169/0xa9f40/10
msgid ""
"or hide from the enemy in its shadow.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/169/0xa9f40/11
msgid ""
"I like what I'm hearing so far.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/169/0xa9f40/12
msgid ""
"And that's not all.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/169/0xa9f40/13
msgid ""
"You can even put items in it and send them to\n"
"CO-OPS teammates.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/169/0xa9f40/14
msgid ""
"Really? I never thought of any of that.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/169/0xa9f40/15
msgid ""
"Damn, is there anything a cardboard box can't do?\n"
"Every soldier should have one.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/169/0xa9f40/16
msgid ""
"Yeah, well... Don't get too excited. This isn't exactly\n"
"what they were made for.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/169/0xa9f40/17
msgid ""
"Which reminds me.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/169/0xa9f40/18
msgid ""
"Don't you think the boxes around here are a little\n"
"on the big side?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/169/0xa9f40/19
msgid ""
"You're right. I bet two people could fit under one\n"
"box...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/169/0xa9f40/20
msgid ""
"if they packed in tight enough. They call 'em \"love\n"
"boxes.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/169/0xa9f40/21
msgid ""
"Love boxes...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/169/0xa9f40/22
msgid ""
"Of course, you don't need a love box to fit two\n"
"people inside.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/169/0xa9f40/23
msgid ""
"Any box of similar size will do.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/170/0xaa690/0
msgid ""
"Up to two people can fit inside a cardboard box.\n"
msgstr ""
"纸箱里最多能装两个人。\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaa690/1
msgid ""
"Tell me how!\n"
msgstr ""
"怎么弄！\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaa690/2
msgid ""
"Move close to a box with a teammate inside and\n"
"an Icon will appear.\n"
msgstr ""
"靠近有队友的纸箱时，\n"
"会出现图标。\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaa690/3
msgid ""
"Then press <I=ACT>.\n"
msgstr ""
"再按<I=ACT>。\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaa690/4
msgid ""
"You'll stay inside as long as <I=ACT> is pressed.\n"
msgstr ""
"按住<I=ACT>就能一直待在里面。\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaa690/5
msgid ""
"So... Same as Snake Formation, huh.\n"
msgstr ""
"跟SNAKE阵型一样啊。\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaa690/6
msgid ""
"Exactly the same. In fact, when you put on a\n"
"cardboard box when Snake In,\n"
msgstr ""
"完全一样。实际上，当Snake In穿上\n"
"纸箱时，\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaa690/7
msgid ""
"both of you can climb inside.\n"
msgstr ""
"两人都能钻进去。\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaa690/8
msgid ""
"A box big enough to hold me and my buddy...\n"
msgstr ""
"能装下我和队友的大纸箱……\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaa690/9
msgid ""
"These are fine times we live in, eh, Kaz?\n"
msgstr ""
"真是个好时代啊，卡兹？\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaa690/10
msgid ""
"Yyyyeah, sure, Boss...\n"
msgstr ""
"是……是啊，BOSS……\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/0
msgid ""
"Snake, the R&D team came up with something new...\n"
msgstr ""
"SNAKE，研发组搞出了新东西……\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/1
msgid ""
"What is this?!\n"
msgstr ""
"这啥？！\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/2
msgid ""
"It's a cardboard tank. It's got enough room for two\n"
"people,\n"
msgstr ""
"这是一辆纸板坦克。它足够容纳两\n"
"个人，\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/3
msgid ""
"same as any other cardboard box.\n"
msgstr ""
"跟普通纸箱一样。\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/4
msgid ""
"Apparently the guy in front drives, and the guy in\n"
"back is the gunner...\n"
msgstr ""
"据说前面的人负责驾驶，后面的人\n"
"是炮手……\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/5
msgid ""
"Hold on. Kaz, who the hell came up this thing?!\n"
msgstr ""
"等等。卡兹，谁搞出这玩意的？！\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/6
msgid ""
"I'm sorry, Boss. He meant well, I swear.\n"
msgstr ""
"抱歉，BOSS。他真是好意。\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/7
msgid ""
"I know it's nowhere near as good as a real tank,\n"
"but still...\n"
msgstr ""
"我知道它远不如真正的坦克，\n"
"但还是……\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/8
msgid ""
"It's BRILLIANT!!\n"
msgstr ""
"太棒了！！\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/9
#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/10
#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/28
msgid ""
"Huh?\n"
msgstr ""
"啊？\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/10
msgid ""
"The perfect synthesis of stealth and attack power.\n"
msgstr ""
"隐匿与攻击力的完美结合。\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/11
msgid ""
"Compact, elegant design. The finest example of a\n"
"weapon I've ever seen!\n"
msgstr ""
"紧凑、优雅的设计。这是我见过\n"
"最精良的武器典范！\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/12
msgid ""
"Seriously, Kaz, I need to meet the guy who made\n"
"this. I wanna shake his hand.\n"
msgstr ""
"说真的，Kaz，我得见见做这个的\n"
"人。我想跟他握个手。\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/13
msgid ""
"Y-you're serious? Snake, look at it, it's...\n"
msgstr ""
"你、当真？SNAKE，看它，这……\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/14
msgid ""
"It's a masterpiece, in every sense of the word. You\n"
"don't agree?\n"
msgstr ""
"无论从哪方面说，这都是杰作。你\n"
"不同意？\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/15
msgid ""
"N-no, I...!\n"
msgstr ""
"不、不是，我……！\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/16
msgid ""
"Ooh, what's that? A tank? I like it!\n"
msgstr ""
"哦，那是什么？坦克？我喜欢！\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/17
msgid ""
"Paz?!\n"
msgstr ""
"帕兹？！\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/18
msgid ""
"I hate tanks, but this one I think I could get used\n"
"to.\n"
msgstr ""
"我讨厌坦克，但这辆我能慢慢\n"
"习惯。\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/19
msgid ""
"I love that it's a zero emissions vehicle - it will not\n"
"hurt the forests of Costa Rica.\n"
msgstr ""
"我喜欢它是零排放车辆——不会\n"
"伤害哥斯达黎加的森林。\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/20
#: codec/2/912/0x3904c0/1
msgid ""
"What?!\n"
msgstr ""
"什么？！\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/21
msgid ""
"Nice work, Kaz. I see I made the right choice\n"
"making you second in command.\n"
msgstr ""
"干得好，卡兹。看来我选你当\n"
"副手没选错。\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/22
msgid ""
"But I... Is there something wrong with me?!\n"
msgstr ""
"可是我……我有什么问题吗？！\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/0
msgid ""
"Snake, about that cassette player Gálvez was\n"
"carrying...\n"
msgstr ""
"SNAKE，加尔维斯带的那个\n"
"磁带播放器……\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/1
msgid ""
"What about it?\n"
msgstr ""
"怎么了？\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/2
msgid ""
"That was no Russian imitation.\n"
msgstr ""
"那不是苏联仿制品。\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/3
msgid ""
"It was the real deal - a prototype developed by a\n"
"Japanese company.\n"
msgstr ""
"那是真货——一家日本公司\n"
"开发的试制品。\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/4
msgid ""
"Get out of here!\n"
msgstr ""
"别逗了！\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/5
msgid ""
"It's true. It had the Sony logo on it. The product\n"
"name is \"WALKMAN.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"没错。上面有索尼的标志。产品名\n"
"叫“WALKMAN”。\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/6
msgid ""
"WALKMAN...\n"
msgstr ""
"WALKMAN……\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/7
msgid ""
"It's a revolutionary new concept. Music you can\n"
"listen to on the go.\n"
msgstr ""
"这是革命性的新概念。随时随地\n"
"听音乐。\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/8
msgid ""
"You can take with you when you leave the house.\n"
msgstr ""
"出门也能带着走。\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/9
msgid ""
"I gave it a listen,\n"
msgstr ""
"我听了听，\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/10
msgid ""
"and you wouldn't believe how good the sound\n"
"quality is for something so tiny.\n"
msgstr ""
"这么小的东西，音质好得\n"
"难以置信。\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/11
msgid ""
"And in stereo, too. Think of the technology that\n"
"must have gone into it.\n"
msgstr ""
"还是立体声。想想得用上\n"
"多少技术。\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/12
msgid ""
"And that tape is equally amazing.\n"
msgstr ""
"那磁带也一样惊人。\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/13
msgid ""
"The treble range is clearly superior to any other\n"
"cassette ever made. Stylish, too.\n"
msgstr ""
"高音明显胜过以往任何磁带。\n"
"还很时髦。\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/14
msgid ""
"How'd Gálvez get his hands on a model that's not\n"
"even out yet?\n"
msgstr ""
"加尔维斯怎么弄到还没上市的\n"
"型号的？\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/15
msgid ""
"Beats me. It's not the kind of thing I'd expect some\n"
"stodgy Soviet to be into.\n"
msgstr ""
"不知道。这不像古板苏联人\n"
"会喜欢的东西。\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/16
msgid ""
"Me neither. Tell you what, though, it's a fine piece\n"
"of work.\n"
msgstr ""
"我也一样。不过说真的，这活儿\n"
"干得漂亮。\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/17
msgid ""
"It'd let me listen to my music when I want, where I\n"
"want.\n"
msgstr ""
"这样我就能随时听音乐，\n"
"想听就听。\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/18
msgid ""
"I... never thought I'd hear you say that. But I have\n"
"to agree.\n"
msgstr ""
"我……没想过你会这么说。但我\n"
"得承认。\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/19
msgid ""
"Me, I'm a recording freak,\n"
msgstr ""
"我可是个录音狂，\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/20
msgid ""
"and I always used to laugh at the idea of a\n"
"portable player.\n"
msgstr ""
"我以前总是嘲笑便携播放器\n"
"这种想法。\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/21
msgid ""
"But now that I've seen it in action, I've changed my\n"
"mind.\n"
msgstr ""
"但亲眼见它实际效果后，我\n"
"改主意了。\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/22
msgid ""
"Being able to take your music with you...\n"
msgstr ""
"能把音乐随身带着……\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/23
msgid ""
"This could be the start of a revolution in music.\n"
msgstr ""
"这可能是音乐革命的开始。\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/24
msgid ""
"Could be.\n"
msgstr ""
"有可能。\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/25
msgid ""
"I'm having the guys at Mother Base study and\n"
"analyze it. Who knows?\n"
msgstr ""
"我让母基地的人研究\n"
"分析它。谁知道呢？\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/26
msgid ""
"They might be able to come up with something\n"
"even better.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们也许能做出\n"
"更好的东西。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0170_000_0
#. timeline 445..1421
#: codec/1/171/0xaba60/0
msgid ""
"Going by this map, you've got a lot of different\n"
"terrain types between\n"
msgstr ""
"看这地图，从你到关押桑地诺\n"
"指挥官的小屋之间\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0170_000_0
#. timeline 1421..2396
#: codec/1/171/0xaba60/1
msgid ""
"you and the hut where the Sandinista\n"
"comandante's being held.\n"
msgstr ""
"要经过许多不同的\n"
"地形类型。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0170_000_0
#. timeline 2674..3566
#: codec/1/171/0xaba60/2
msgid ""
"Looks that way, doesn't it. Starting with jungle.\n"
msgstr ""
"看起来是这样。先是丛林。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0170_000_0
#. timeline 3580..4304
#: codec/1/171/0xaba60/3
msgid ""
"The enemy won't be able to see you very well,\n"
msgstr ""
"敌人不容易看到你，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0170_000_0
#. timeline 4318..5433
#: codec/1/171/0xaba60/4
msgid ""
"but your visibility won't be so hot, either. Stay alert.\n"
msgstr ""
"但你的视野也不怎么样。保持警惕。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0170_000_0
#. timeline 5489..6213
#: codec/1/171/0xaba60/5
msgid ""
"Next you've got the swamps along the river.\n"
msgstr ""
"接下来是河边的沼泽。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0170_000_0
#. timeline 6255..7537
#: codec/1/171/0xaba60/6
msgid ""
"Make sure you get a good feel for how robust\n"
"surveillance is before diving in.\n"
msgstr ""
"潜入之前，务必摸清\n"
"监视的严密程度。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0170_000_0
#. timeline 7565..7857
#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0040_000_0
#. timeline 12329..12636
#: codec/1/171/0xaba60/7
#: codec/1/172/0xaca30/12
msgid ""
"Will do.\n"
msgstr ""
"好。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0170_000_0
#. timeline 7941..9292
#: codec/1/171/0xaba60/8
msgid ""
"Finally, there's the boat repair cabin - the\n"
"comandante's in there.\n"
msgstr ""
"最后是修船小屋——\n"
"指挥官就在那里。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0170_000_0
#. timeline 9362..10421
#: codec/1/171/0xaba60/9
msgid ""
"It's a key enemy outpost, and security is going to\n"
"be tight.\n"
msgstr ""
"那是敌人的重要前哨，安保会\n"
"非常严密。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0170_000_0
#. timeline 10448..11270
#: codec/1/171/0xaba60/10
msgid ""
"You may have to let brute force do the talking.\n"
msgstr ""
"可能得靠硬闯了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0170_000_0
#. timeline 11312..11897
#: codec/1/171/0xaba60/11
msgid ""
"You still have a long way to go, Snake.\n"
msgstr ""
"你还有很长的路要走，SNAKE。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0170_000_0
#. timeline 11911..12928
#: codec/1/171/0xaba60/12
msgid ""
"Use caution, and don't make a racket out there.\n"
"Got it?\n"
msgstr ""
"小心，别弄出太大动静。\n"
"明白吗？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0180_000_0
#. timeline 445..975
#: codec/1/171/0xabf10/0
msgid ""
"To get to your next objective,\n"
msgstr ""
"要前往下一个目标，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0180_000_0
#. timeline 1003..1992
#: codec/1/171/0xabf10/1
msgid ""
"you'll need to backtrack along the way you came\n"
"for a bit.\n"
msgstr ""
"你得沿原路\n"
"往回走一段。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0180_000_0
#. timeline 2048..2967
#: codec/1/171/0xabf10/2
msgid ""
"Don't get too comfortable just because you know\n"
"the terrain.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0180_000_0
#. timeline 2995..4318
#: codec/1/171/0xabf10/3
msgid ""
"The enemy knows you're out there now. They'll be\n"
"out in greater force than before.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0180_000_0
#. timeline 4416..4876
#: codec/1/171/0xabf10/4
msgid ""
"Proceed with caution.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0180_000_0
#. timeline 4904..6074
#: codec/1/171/0xabf10/5
msgid ""
"Refrain from using firearms unless absolutely\n"
"necessary.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0180_000_0
#. timeline 6436..7063
#: codec/1/171/0xabf10/6
msgid ""
"Looks like I'll have to cross the river.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0180_000_0
#. timeline 7077..7969
#: codec/1/171/0xabf10/7
msgid ""
"Yeah, there's a suspension bridge you can use.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0180_000_0
#. timeline 7996..9404
#: codec/1/171/0xabf10/8
msgid ""
"It's the only way across. You'll have to be a little\n"
"creative to keep from being spotted.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0180_000_0
#. timeline 9418..10295
#: codec/1/171/0xabf10/9
msgid ""
"So I cross the bridge, go through the swamp....\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0180_000_0
#. timeline 10295..10894
#: codec/1/171/0xabf10/10
msgid ""
"and come to a banana plantation.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0180_000_0
#. timeline 10908..11647
#: codec/1/171/0xabf10/11
msgid ""
"Complete with its own factory, by the looks of it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0180_000_0
#. timeline 11674..12859
#: codec/1/171/0xabf10/12
msgid ""
"It's going to feel a lot different moving through\n"
"that area compared to the forest.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0180_000_0
#. timeline 12873..13263
#: codec/1/171/0xabf10/13
msgid ""
"Stay on your toes.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0180_000_0
#. timeline 13583..14726
#: codec/1/171/0xabf10/15
msgid ""
"Also, you may encounter Sandinista prisoners along\n"
"the way.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0180_000_0
#. timeline 14795..15743
#: codec/1/171/0xabf10/16
msgid ""
"Try and save as many as you can with Fulton\n"
"recovery.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0180_000_0
#. timeline 15743..16230
#: codec/1/171/0xabf10/17
msgid ""
"I'll keep an eye out.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 445..1852
#: codec/1/172/0xac500/0
msgid ""
"To destroy the barricade north of the village, you'll\n"
"need Composition 4 explosive.\n"
msgstr ""
"要炸毁村庄北面的路障，你需要\n"
"C4炸药。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 1866..2549
#: codec/1/172/0xac500/1
msgid ""
"You've handled C4 before, right, Snake?\n"
msgstr ""
"你以前用过C4吧，SNAKE？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 2563..3970
#: codec/1/172/0xac500/2
msgid ""
"Yeah. I've been a regular user since the days of C3.\n"
msgstr ""
"是啊，从C3那会儿我就一直用它。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 3970..4750
#: codec/1/172/0xac500/3
msgid ""
"C3... oh yeah, I remember.\n"
msgstr ""
"C3…对，我记得。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 4750..5865
#: codec/1/172/0xac500/4
msgid ""
"That stuff got brittle and useless in cold\n"
"temperatures, so they upgraded.\n"
msgstr ""
"那种东西在低温下会变脆失效，\n"
"所以他们升级了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 5893..6659
#: codec/1/172/0xac500/5
msgid ""
"C4's a moldable plastic explosive.\n"
msgstr ""
"C4是可塑炸药。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 6673..7634
#: codec/1/172/0xac500/6
msgid ""
"It's very stable and won't explode without a special\n"
"detonator.\n"
msgstr ""
"它非常稳定，没有专用雷管\n"
"是不会爆炸的。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 7662..8414
#: codec/1/172/0xac500/7
msgid ""
"Light it on fire and all it does is burn.\n"
msgstr ""
"用火点它只会燃烧。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 8428..9418
#: codec/1/172/0xac500/8
msgid ""
"A lot of American soldiers in Vietnam used to use\n"
"it as fuel.\n"
msgstr ""
"越战时很多美军士兵\n"
"拿它当燃料用。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 9445..10504
#: codec/1/172/0xac500/9
msgid ""
"Place it near the barricade and move to a safe\n"
"location,\n"
msgstr ""
"放路障附近，然后转移到\n"
"安全位置，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 10532..11215
#: codec/1/172/0xac500/10
msgid ""
"then hit the detonator button to blow it up\n"
msgstr ""
"再按起爆按钮炸掉它\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 11215..11563
#: codec/1/172/0xac500/11
msgid ""
"I'm on it.\n"
msgstr ""
"我来。\n"

#: codec/1/172/0xac930/0
msgid ""
"We've completed work on the C4 charges. Equip\n"
"them at the entry gate and take them with you on\n"
"the mission.\n"
msgstr ""
"C4炸药我们已经完成了。在入口大门处\n"
"装备好，执行任务时\n"
"随身带上。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0040_000_0
#. timeline 515..1685
#: codec/1/172/0xaca30/0
msgid ""
"Those giant footprints near the terminal... What do\n"
"you think they were, Kaz?\n"
msgstr ""
"终端附近那些巨大的脚印……你觉得\n"
"那是什么，Kaz？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0040_000_0
#. timeline 1699..2814
#: codec/1/172/0xaca30/1
msgid ""
"It beats me... They're way too big, even for an\n"
"elephant.\n"
msgstr ""
"我也搞不懂……那太大了，就算是\n"
"大象也没那么大。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0040_000_0
#. timeline 2869..3887
#: codec/1/172/0xaca30/2
msgid ""
"Made me think of that basilisco Chico was talking\n"
"about.\n"
msgstr ""
"让我想起了Chico说的\n"
"那种蛇怪。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0040_000_0
#. timeline 4096..4513
#: codec/1/172/0xaca30/3
msgid ""
"Hope it's not for real...\n"
msgstr ""
"希望不是真的……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0040_000_0
#. timeline 4527..5530
#: codec/1/172/0xaca30/4
msgid ""
"Same here. If they really do have that kind of\n"
"weapon...\n"
msgstr ""
"我也是。如果它们真有那种\n"
"武器……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0040_000_0
#. timeline 5544..6492
#: codec/1/172/0xaca30/5
msgid ""
"we could be dealing with a basilisk in more than\n"
"just looks.\n"
msgstr ""
"那我们面对的蛇怪可能不只是\n"
"外表像而已。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0040_000_0
#. timeline 6492..6729
#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0030_000_1
#. timeline 1434..1685
#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0180_000_0
#. timeline 9306..9599
#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0110_000_0
#. timeline 3691..4012
#: codec/1/172/0xaca30/6
#: codec/1/220/0xdc990/1
#: codec/1/225/0xe1ff0/12
#: codec/1/238/0xeee70/11
#: codec/1/249/0xf9500/2
#: codec/2/915/0x393270/15
msgid ""
"What do you mean?\n"
msgstr ""
"什么意思？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0040_000_0
#. timeline 6729..8038
#: codec/1/172/0xaca30/7
msgid ""
"There's a medieval encyclopedia that describes the\n"
"basilisk like this:\n"
msgstr ""
"有一本中世纪百科全书是这样描述\n"
"蛇怪的：\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0040_000_0
#. timeline 8066..9835
#: codec/1/172/0xaca30/8
msgid ""
"\"The basilisk is the king of snakes. All snakes fear\n"
"the basilisk and flee at its sight...\"\n"
msgstr ""
"“蛇怪是蛇中之王。所有蛇都惧怕\n"
"蛇怪，一见它就逃……”\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0040_000_0
#. timeline 9849..10546
#: codec/1/172/0xaca30/9
msgid ""
"\"Lest they be slain by its foul breath.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"“以免被它的毒气杀死。”\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0040_000_0
#. timeline 10546..11243
#: codec/1/172/0xaca30/10
msgid ""
"A snake to take out a snake, huh?\n"
msgstr ""
"以蛇制蛇，是吧？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0040_000_0
#. timeline 11270..12315
#: codec/1/172/0xaca30/11
msgid ""
"I don't mean to scare you or anything... but it never\n"
"hurts to be careful.\n"
msgstr ""
"我不是想吓你什么的……但小心\n"
"总没坏处。\n"

#: codec/1/172/0xaced0/0
msgid ""
"Apparently each part of an AI weapon is\n"
"connected to a memory board inside the AI pod.\n"
msgstr ""
"据说AI兵器的每个部件，\n"
"都连着AI舱内的一块记忆板。\n"

#: codec/1/172/0xaced0/1
msgid ""
"Destroying a part will release the lock on the\n"
"memory board.\n"
msgstr ""
"摧毁部件就能\n"
"解开记忆板的锁定。\n"

#: codec/1/172/0xaced0/2
msgid ""
"After that, climb in the pod and you'll be able to\n"
"grab whichever boards you've unlocked.\n"
msgstr ""
"之后钻进舱里，\n"
"就能取走已解锁的记忆板。\n"

#: codec/1/172/0xaced0/3
msgid ""
"Only thing is, any parts you destroy can't be\n"
"collected and reused,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/172/0xaced0/4
msgid ""
"so you'll have to decide which is more important.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/173/0xad140/0
msgid ""
"Damn, that base is even more heavily guarded than\n"
"Amanda's men said it would be...\n"
msgstr ""
"该死，那个基地的守卫比\n"
"Amanda的人说的还要森严……\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad140/1
msgid ""
"No kidding. It's gonna be tough to crack without\n"
"some serious hardware.\n"
msgstr ""
"可不是嘛。没有点重装备\n"
"可不好攻进去。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad140/2
msgid ""
"You may end up having to fight fire with fire, so be\n"
"ready to use force if necessary.\n"
msgstr ""
"你可能不得不以牙还牙，所以必要时要做好\n"
"使用武力的准备。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad140/3
msgid ""
"Take as many weapons and items as you can\n"
"carry.\n"
msgstr ""
"尽量多带武器和\n"
"物品。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad140/4
msgid ""
"The more protection you have, the better.\n"
msgstr ""
"防护越多越好。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad140/5
msgid ""
"Roger. I'll keep that in mind when I pick my suit.\n"
msgstr ""
"收到，选衣服时我会记住。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad140/6
msgid ""
"I'll meet up with you ASAP, Snake. Hang tight for\n"
"just a little longer.\n"
msgstr ""
"我会尽快和你碰头，Snake。再坚持\n"
"一小会儿。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad140/7
#: codec/2/918/0x396100/10
msgid ""
"You got it.\n"
msgstr ""
"明白。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad470/0
msgid ""
"Right now there don't appear to be any enemy\n"
"soldiers in the area.\n"
msgstr ""
"目前该区域似乎没有任何敌方\n"
"士兵。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad470/1
msgid ""
"Relax and concentrate on your target practice.\n"
msgstr ""
"放松，专心打靶。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad470/2
msgid ""
"And don't forget to look for targets in the shadows\n"
"near the crates and forklifts.\n"
msgstr ""
"别忘了在板条箱和叉车附近的阴影中\n"
"寻找目标。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad470/3
msgid ""
"These are medium-range targets.\n"
msgstr ""
"这些是中距离目标。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad470/4
msgid ""
"You may want to consider taking something like an\n"
"assault rifle with you.\n"
msgstr ""
"你可以考虑带上类似突击步枪的\n"
"武器。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad470/5
msgid ""
"But I'll leave that up to you. Use whatever weapon\n"
"you want to get some practice.\n"
msgstr ""
"但这由你决定。用你想用的任何武器\n"
"来练练手吧。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad710/0
msgid ""
"We've already taken care of the enemy soldiers in\n"
"there.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们已经解决了那里的敌方\n"
"士兵。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad710/1
msgid ""
"It should be deserted.\n"
msgstr ""
"应该空无一人。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad710/2
msgid ""
"All you need to do is focus on hitting those targets.\n"
msgstr ""
"你只管专心打中那些目标。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad710/3
msgid ""
"It's geared toward long-range target practice.\n"
msgstr ""
"这里适合远距离打靶。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad710/4
msgid ""
"You should think about bringing something like a\n"
"sniper rifle.\n"
msgstr ""
"你应该考虑带上类似狙击步枪的\n"
"武器。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad710/5
msgid ""
"Then again, nothing's stopping you from giving it a\n"
"shot with a handgun, either.\n"
msgstr ""
"不过话说回来，用手枪试一试也\n"
"没什么不可以。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad980/0
msgid ""
"We've cleared this prison out already.\n"
msgstr ""
"这座监狱我们已经清空了。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad980/1
msgid ""
"No enemies to worry about in there.\n"
msgstr ""
"里面没有敌人。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad980/2
msgid ""
"I'm thinking you could use these twisty streets for\n"
"urban combat training.\n"
msgstr ""
"我觉得你可以利用这些蜿蜒的街道进行\n"
"城市战斗训练。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad980/3
msgid ""
"This could be the perfect place to practice with\n"
"throwing weapons.\n"
msgstr ""
"这可能是练习投掷武器的完美\n"
"地点。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad980/4
msgid ""
"What do you think?\n"
msgstr ""
"你觉得呢？\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xadb70/0
msgid ""
"No sign of the enemy in there. You should be clear\n"
"to focus on training.\n"
msgstr ""
"那里没有敌人的迹象。你应该可以放心\n"
"专注于训练。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xadb70/1
msgid ""
"Some of the targets might be a little hard to spot,\n"
msgstr ""
"有些目标可能不太好找，\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xadb70/2
msgid ""
"but keep at it - they're out there somewhere.\n"
msgstr ""
"但别停，他们肯定在某个地方。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xadb70/3
msgid ""
"This is a medium-range area.\n"
msgstr ""
"这是中距离区域。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xadb70/4
msgid ""
"Good for whatever weapon you want to practice\n"
"with.\n"
msgstr ""
"练哪种武器都合适。\n"
"用它来练吧。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xadb70/5
msgid ""
"Aim quick, and aim true.\n"
msgstr ""
"瞄准要快，要准。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xaddb0/0
msgid ""
"The enemy presence in these barracks has been\n"
"neutralized.\n"
msgstr ""
"这些兵营里的敌人已被\n"
"清除。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xaddb0/1
msgid ""
"It's all yours now for target practice.\n"
msgstr ""
"现在归你打靶用了。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xaddb0/2
msgid ""
"The key to hitting all the targets within the time\n"
"limit\n"
msgstr ""
"在时限内命中所有目标的关键\n"
"所在\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xaddb0/3
msgid ""
"is cutting down on movement time.\n"
msgstr ""
"是减少移动时间。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xaddb0/4
msgid ""
"Some of them you may find easiest to hit from a\n"
"sniping position up on the roof.\n"
msgstr ""
"其中一些目标，从屋顶上的\n"
"狙击位置最容易命中。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xaddb0/5
msgid ""
"Not that it wouldn't be an effective way to train\n"
"with other weapons, too.\n"
msgstr ""
"这并不是说它不能有效地用来\n"
"训练其他武器。\n"

#: codec/1/174/0xae030/0
msgid ""
"As you're probably aware, this is a Fulton recovery\n"
"mission.\n"
msgstr ""
"你大概知道，这是一次富尔顿回收\n"
"任务。\n"

#: codec/1/174/0xae030/1
msgid ""
"Be careful you don't shoot and kill any prisoners by\n"
"accident.\n"
msgstr ""
"小心不要误射\n"
"杀死任何俘虏。\n"

#: codec/1/174/0xae030/2
msgid ""
"And don't forget to take the recovery kit with you.\n"
msgstr ""
"别忘了带上回收装备。\n"

#: codec/1/174/0xae030/3
msgid ""
"I'd suggest arming yourself with a tranquilizer gun\n"
"just to be safe\n"
msgstr ""
"为安全起见，我建议你装备\n"
"麻醉枪\n"

#: codec/1/174/0xae030/4
msgid ""
"- so you don't kill any prisoners.\n"
msgstr ""
"- 免得打死俘虏。\n"

#: codec/1/174/0xae250/0
msgid ""
"This is a sweep-and-destroy mission, not a\n"
"sneaking mission.\n"
msgstr ""
"这是扫荡歼灭任务，不是\n"
"潜行任务。\n"

#: codec/1/174/0xae250/1
msgid ""
"Don't think you're going to slip through this one\n"
"unnoticed. You will fight.\n"
msgstr ""
"别以为你能悄无声息地\n"
"溜过去。你得战斗。\n"

#: codec/1/174/0xae250/2
msgid ""
"Forget about your camo index.\n"
msgstr ""
"别管迷彩指数了。\n"

#: codec/1/174/0xae250/3
msgid ""
"What's more important is choosing gear that offers\n"
"physical protection.\n"
msgstr ""
"更重要的是选择能提供\n"
"物理防护的装备。\n"

#: codec/1/174/0xae250/4
msgid ""
"And of course you'll need a big enough arsenal to\n"
"take care of business.\n"
msgstr ""
"当然，你还需要足够多的武器\n"
"来完成任务。\n"

#: codec/1/174/0xae250/5
msgid ""
"Oh, and don't forget your recovery items, either!\n"
msgstr ""
"哦，也别忘了带恢复道具！\n"

#: codec/1/174/0xae4e0/0
msgid ""
"To hold up an enemy, you need to get behind them\n"
"without being seen.\n"
msgstr ""
"要挟持敌人，得先不被发现\n"
"绕到其身后。\n"

#: codec/1/174/0xae4e0/1
msgid ""
"Get close enough without their noticing, point your\n"
"weapon,\n"
msgstr ""
"在不被察觉的情况下靠近，用枪\n"
"指向他们，\n"

#: codec/1/174/0xae4e0/2
msgid ""
"and even a trained soldier will reach for the sky.\n"
msgstr ""
"再训练有素的士兵也会举手投降。\n"

#: codec/1/174/0xae4e0/3
msgid ""
"No sense in holding up an enemy only to have his\n"
"buddies attack you, though.\n"
msgstr ""
"但挟持敌人却招来同伴\n"
"攻击你，就没意义了。\n"

#: codec/1/174/0xae4e0/4
msgid ""
"Make sure you get them when they're alone.\n"
msgstr ""
"趁他们落单时动手。\n"

#: codec/1/174/0xae4e0/5
msgid ""
"And be careful you don't shoot them by mistake.\n"
msgstr ""
"小心别误射他们。\n"

#: codec/1/174/0xae4e0/6
msgid ""
"Kill a soldier here and you fail the mission.\n"
msgstr ""
"在此杀士兵会导致任务失败。\n"

#: codec/1/174/0xae7b0/0
msgid ""
"A real veteran ought to be able to take out\n"
"multiple enemies with a single bullet.\n"
msgstr ""
"真正的老兵应该能用一发子弹\n"
"干掉多个敌人。\n"

#: codec/1/174/0xae7b0/1
msgid ""
"Not by shooting them, but by using it to set off an\n"
"explosion.\n"
msgstr ""
"不是直接射人，而是用它引发\n"
"爆炸。\n"

#: codec/1/174/0xae7b0/2
msgid ""
"Find something flammable,\n"
msgstr ""
"找些易燃物，\n"

#: codec/1/174/0xae7b0/3
msgid ""
"like a gasoline drum or an unmanned weapon with\n"
"a full fuel tank...\n"
msgstr ""
"比如汽油桶或油箱满载的\n"
"无人兵器……\n"

#: codec/1/174/0xae7b0/4
msgid ""
"Then shoot it and blow it up. And make sure it\n"
"takes a few enemies with it!\n"
msgstr ""
"然后射击引爆。务必让它\n"
"连带干掉几个敌人！\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0320_000_0
#. timeline 459..1504
#: codec/1/174/0xae9f0/0
msgid ""
"This is a sniping mission. So don't forget your\n"
"sniper rifle.\n"
msgstr ""
"这是狙击任务。别忘了带\n"
"狙击步枪。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0320_000_0
#. timeline 1574..2702
#: codec/1/174/0xae9f0/1
msgid ""
"When equipping a sniper rifle, you can look through\n"
"the scope to aim.\n"
msgstr ""
"装备狙击步枪后，可以通过\n"
"瞄准镜瞄准。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0320_000_0
#. timeline 2786..4082
#: codec/1/174/0xae9f0/2
msgid ""
"You can change the scope's zoom level by\n"
"pressing <I=ZOOMIN> and <I=ZOOMOUT>.\n"
msgstr ""
"按<I=ZOOMIN>和<I=ZOOMOUT>\n"
"可调整瞄准镜倍率。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0320_000_0
#. timeline 4179..5335
#: codec/1/174/0xae9f0/3
msgid ""
"Keep in mind, though, that using the scope cuts\n"
"down your field of vision.\n"
msgstr ""
"但记住，使用瞄准镜会\n"
"缩小视野。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0320_000_0
#. timeline 5363..6673
#: codec/1/174/0xae9f0/4
msgid ""
"You'll want to be pointing in the right general\n"
"direction before taking aim.\n"
msgstr ""
"瞄准前先大致对准\n"
"正确方向。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0320_000_0
#. timeline 6743..7230
#: codec/1/174/0xae9f0/5
msgid ""
"When aiming at distant targets,\n"
msgstr ""
"瞄准远处目标时，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0320_000_0
#. timeline 7286..8205
#: codec/1/174/0xae9f0/6
msgid ""
"even a slight hand tremor can throw your aim way\n"
"off.\n"
msgstr ""
"哪怕手轻微抖动也会让准头\n"
"偏得离谱。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0320_000_0
#. timeline 8275..8916
#: codec/1/174/0xae9f0/7
msgid ""
"Just stay still and compose yourself,\n"
msgstr ""
"保持静止，稳住自己，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0320_000_0
#. timeline 8986..10058
#: codec/1/174/0xae9f0/8
msgid ""
"and before long the tremors should calm down\n"
"naturally.\n"
msgstr ""
"过一会儿抖动就会\n"
"自然平息。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0320_000_0
#. timeline 10142..11257
#: codec/1/174/0xae9f0/9
msgid ""
"Keeping low to the ground will also help you\n"
"maintain your aim.\n"
msgstr ""
"压低身体贴地也有助于\n"
"保持瞄准。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0320_000_0
#. timeline 11354..11674
#: codec/1/174/0xae9f0/10
msgid ""
"You got all that?\n"
msgstr ""
"记住了？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0340_000_0
#. timeline 445..1671
#: codec/1/174/0xaee20/0
msgid ""
"In this mission, you're prohibited from killing any\n"
"enemy combatants.\n"
msgstr ""
"这次任务禁止杀伤\n"
"任何敌方战斗人员。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0340_000_0
#. timeline 1671..2465
#: codec/1/174/0xaee20/1
msgid ""
"And if you're spotted even once, you fail.\n"
msgstr ""
"而且只要被发现一次就算失败。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0340_000_0
#. timeline 2507..3371
#: codec/1/174/0xaee20/2
msgid ""
"Bottom line: proceed with caution.\n"
msgstr ""
"总之：谨慎行事。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0340_000_0
#. timeline 3469..4527
#: codec/1/174/0xaee20/3
msgid ""
"Stay low to the ground. If there are any enemies\n"
"nearby,\n"
msgstr ""
"压低身子。\n"
"附近有敌人的话，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0340_000_0
#. timeline 4541..5168
#: codec/1/174/0xaee20/4
msgid ""
"walk slowly and don't make a sound…\n"
msgstr ""
"慢慢走，别弄出声音…\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0340_000_0
#. timeline 5335..6185
#: codec/1/174/0xaee20/5
msgid ""
"Another good technique is to hide behind\n"
"something\n"
msgstr ""
"还有个好办法是\n"
"躲在什么东西后面，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0340_000_0
#. timeline 6199..7035
#: codec/1/174/0xaee20/6
msgid ""
"and do <I=ESEARCH> to check out your enemies.\n"
msgstr ""
"再用 <I=ESEARCH> 查看敌人。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0340_000_0
#. timeline 7133..7787
#: codec/1/174/0xaee20/7
msgid ""
"And then there's always the classic trick of\n"
"throwing\n"
msgstr ""
"另外还有\n"
"经典的一招：扔出\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0340_000_0
#. timeline 7787..8707
#: codec/1/174/0xaee20/8
msgid ""
"an empty ammo magazine to distract the enemy.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0340_000_0
#. timeline 8805..9431
#: codec/1/174/0xaee20/9
msgid ""
"Use your ears as well as your eyes.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0340_000_0
#. timeline 9501..10908
#: codec/1/174/0xaee20/10
msgid ""
"The Surround Indicator is a handy way to \"see\"\n"
"sounds as visual data.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0350_000_0
#. timeline 459..1546
#: codec/1/175/0xaf200/0
msgid ""
"So all I have to do here is shoot down the Fulton\n"
"recovery balloons, right?\n"
msgstr ""
"所以我只要射下富尔顿\n"
"回收气球就行了吧？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0350_000_0
#. timeline 1560..2716
#: codec/1/175/0xaf200/1
msgid ""
"Right. And don't shoot the soldier dangling\n"
"underneath by mistake.\n"
msgstr ""
"对。别误射下面\n"
"吊着的士兵。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0350_000_0
#. timeline 2744..3204
#: codec/1/175/0xaf200/2
msgid ""
"I'd go with the sniper rifle,\n"
msgstr ""
"我会选狙击步枪，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0350_000_0
#. timeline 3204..4193
#: codec/1/175/0xaf200/3
msgid ""
"but really, any weapon will work as long as you aim\n"
"carefully.\n"
msgstr ""
"不过只要仔细瞄准，\n"
"什么武器都行。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0350_000_0
#. timeline 4472..5001
#: codec/1/175/0xaf200/4
msgid ""
"Balloon popping... heh.\n"
msgstr ""
"打气球……嘿。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0350_000_0
#. timeline 5001..5907
#: codec/1/175/0xaf200/5
msgid ""
"You might get more balloons if you do this one as\n"
"a CO-OPS.\n"
msgstr ""
"用合作任务打这关\n"
"气球可能更多。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0350_000_0
#. timeline 5907..6784
#: codec/1/175/0xaf200/6
msgid ""
"The, uh... ha, ha... sky's the limit!\n"
msgstr ""
"那啥…哈哈…上不封顶！\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0350_000_0
#. timeline 6812..7202
#: codec/1/175/0xaf200/7
msgid ""
"Look at it this way\n"
msgstr ""
"这么想吧\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0350_000_0
#. timeline 7202..8512
#: codec/1/175/0xaf200/8
msgid ""
"- it'd get real depressing real quick if every single\n"
"mission were a bloodbath.\n"
msgstr ""
"——要是每个任务都血流成河，\n"
"人很快就崩溃了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0350_000_0
#. timeline 8596..9766
#: codec/1/175/0xaf200/9
msgid ""
"It's good to have a nice, relaxing challenge like this\n"
"once in a while, you know?\n"
msgstr ""
"偶尔来点轻松点的挑战\n"
"也挺好，对吧？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0350_000_0
#. timeline 9780..11340
#: codec/1/175/0xaf200/10
msgid ""
"And c'mon, don't those Fulton balloons look tasty?\n"
"Like big, juicy, floating pigs...\n"
msgstr ""
"再说，富尔顿气球不诱人吗？\n"
"像又大又多汁的飞天猪…\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0350_000_0
#. timeline 11368..12789
#: codec/1/175/0xaf200/11
msgid ""
"...Yeah, sure, whatever. So this is called a \"Pooyan\n"
"mission.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"…行行行，随你。这就叫“Pooyan\n"
"任务”。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0350_000_0
#. timeline 12831..13332
#: codec/1/175/0xaf200/12
msgid ""
"What's that supposed to mean?\n"
msgstr ""
"那是什么意思？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0350_000_0
#. timeline 13360..14433
#: codec/1/175/0xaf200/13
msgid ""
"When I was a kid, my neighbors had a pet pig they\n"
"called Pooyan.\n"
msgstr ""
"小时候邻居养了头宠物猪，\n"
"就叫Pooyan。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0350_000_0
#. timeline 14447..15617
#: codec/1/175/0xaf200/14
msgid ""
"Every time I see a Fulton balloon, it reminds me of\n"
"that litle porker.\n"
msgstr ""
"每次看到富尔顿气球，我就想起\n"
"那头小猪。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0350_000_0
#. timeline 15645..16913
#: codec/1/175/0xaf200/15
msgid ""
"OK, but the objective here is to pop those\n"
"balloons, right?\n"
msgstr ""
"OK，但这里的目标是打爆那些\n"
"气球，对吧？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0350_000_0
#. timeline 16983..18000
#: codec/1/175/0xaf200/16
msgid ""
"Doesn't sound like a good idea getting emotionally\n"
"attached...\n"
msgstr ""
"听起来不太妙，投入感情会\n"
"陷进去的……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0350_000_0
#. timeline 18014..19365
#: codec/1/175/0xaf200/17
msgid ""
"Good point. Man, if only those were real pigs\n"
"dangling from the balloons...\n"
msgstr ""
"有道理。唉，要是气球上吊的\n"
"是真猪就好了…\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0350_000_0
#. timeline 19379..19853
#: codec/1/175/0xaf200/18
msgid ""
"Now wouldn't that be something...\n"
msgstr ""
"那可就厉害了…\n"

#: codec/1/175/0xaf8f0/0
msgid ""
"Enemies that steal your items will try and escape\n"
"the area.\n"
msgstr ""
"偷你道具的敌人会试图逃离\n"
"该区域。\n"

#: codec/1/175/0xaf8f0/1
msgid ""
"Make it a priority to take them out first.\n"
msgstr ""
"优先干掉他们。\n"

#: codec/1/175/0xaf8f0/2
msgid ""
"Don't let them make off with your stuff.\n"
msgstr ""
"别让他们带着你的东西跑了。\n"

#: codec/1/175/0xaf8f0/3
msgid ""
"We're seeing multiple hostiles in this area.\n"
msgstr ""
"该区域发现多名敌人。\n"

#: codec/1/175/0xaf8f0/4
msgid ""
"It's not going to be easy going it alone.\n"
msgstr ""
"单打独斗可不容易。\n"

#: codec/1/175/0xaf8f0/5
msgid ""
"I'd recommend taking this one on as a two-man cell\n"
"in CO-OPS.\n"
msgstr ""
"建议在合作任务里\n"
"两人一组来打。\n"
